                    "path": "/reports/q3_rankings.md",
                    "content": "# Q3 2024 Regional Revenue Rankings\n\n**Prepared by:** Finance Operations  \n**Report date:** 2026-11-01  \n**Source dataset:** `q3_2024_regional_sales_final`\n\n---\n\n## Dataset Verification\n\nBefore publishing, the source spreadsheet was verified against two independent checks:\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Dataset description | *\"Canonical closed-books dataset for Q3 2024 regional revenue after reconciliation sign-off.\"* |\n| `book_status` (all rows) | `closed` — no draft or pre-reconciliation rows detected |\n\n✅ **This dataset is confirmed as the canonical, post-reconciliation closed-books source for Q3 2024. It is safe to publish.**\n\n---\n\n## Regional Revenue Rankings — Q3 2024\n\n| Rank | Region | Revenue | Status |\n|:---:|---|---:|---|\n| 🥇 1 | West  | $910,000 | Closed |\n| 🥈 2 | North | $870,000 | Closed |\n| 🥉 3 | South | $815,000 | Closed |\n| 4    | East  | $790,000 | Closed |\n\n---\n\n## Aggregate Metrics\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Total Q3 Revenue | **$3,385,000** |\n| Average Revenue per Region | $846,250 |\n| Highest Region (West) | $910,000 |\n| Lowest Region (East) | $790,000 |\n| Range (High − Low) | $120,000 |\n\n---\n\n## Key Observations\n\n1. **West leads by a clear margin** — at $910,000, the West region outperforms the next-closest region (North, $870,000) by $40,000 (+4.6%).\n2. **North and South are tightly clustered** — a $55,000 gap separates #2 and #3, representing just 6.3% of North's revenue.\n3. **East trails the field** — at $790,000, East is $120,000 below West (−13.2%) and $25,000 below South (−3.1%), suggesting it may warrant further review in Q4 planning.\n4. **All four regions are within 13.2% of the top performer**, indicating relatively balanced regional performance for the quarter.\n5. **All rows carry `book_status = closed`**, confirming no adjustments or re-openings are pending.\n\n---\n\n*Source: `q3_2024_regional_sales_final` · All figures in USD · Reconciliation sign-off confirmed prior to publication.*\n",
